From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:46:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(ui): another setup's WCS triad stays on its spot of
 the part

With two setups holding the part differently, the viewport drew the
other setup's WCS at its raw stored place (in its own setup's frame),
off the part. `setup_relative::wcs_view_pose` now maps it through
`transform_between(owner, active)` - the transform the part itself
goes through - and the gizmo builder draws that pose; a refused
transform hides the triad instead of drawing it somewhere wrong. The
active setup's own WCS and setup-less documents are unchanged.

Pinned by wcs_view_pose (app, 3 tests) and
wcs_gizmo_tests::another_setups_wcs_triad_rides_the_part_into_the_shown_setup
(ui; fails with the mapping disabled).

Fixes #558

